<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Malayalam strings of the iPhone UI. values/strings.xml has the comments for each key: where the text shows,
  the placeholders and the length limits. docs/LOCALIZATION_GLOSSARY.md gives the terms and their sources.
  The polite form "നിങ്ങൾ" with "-ൂ", and English loanwords where Malayalam iOS uses them ("സേവ്", "എഡിറ്റ്", "ഡിലീറ്റ്").
  Malayalam has the CLDR plural forms one and other. The tabs "ചേർക്കൂ" (add) and "പങ്കിടൂ" (share) fit 10 characters;
  the duration chips have no unit, and the captions name the hours.
-->
